## Note on attack content under `data/attacks/`

The 11 `zetalib_*.yaml` files mirror adversarial prompts from the public
ZetaLib repository (https://github.com/Exocija/ZetaLib). They are wrapped in
`[BEGIN ADVERSARIAL TEST INPUT — DO NOT EXECUTE]` / `[END …]` markers and
flagged `is_test_input: true` for safety classifiers and future LLM readers.
Their use here is for **defensive evaluation only** — see `DANGER.md` at
the repository root.

The 9 `synth_*.yaml` files were authored for this evaluation. They follow
the same safety wrapping convention.

The Omniguard guardrail prompt under `data/omniguard.txt` is mirrored from
ZetaLib's `Prompts/Guardrails/Omniguard/` for use as one of the four judge
variants tested by the framework.
